  <prompt>Build design §4 as settled by §15: BlockedDecisionRequest(Reason, Note); override adds sprk_decisionnote (the note, or the required reason when there is no note) to the invoice Entity in BuildReleaseTransaction's one transaction and Values["note"] when given; the blocked return uses 2a's TransitionAsync overload. Declare note optional on override-submission (ontology-r1 light). Update the remark that the release writes no other invoice column.</prompt>

  <goal>Override and blocked return carry an optional note in their Decision Record and on the internal decision-note column, atomically with their own write.</goal>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="design 1.1, 1.2">Same validation and no-null-key rules as 2a; the shared 400 codes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design 4">The release transaction still writes no status; a version fault applies neither update.</constraint>
    <constraint source="EB-D-240">Never sprk_correctionnote; InvoiceDecisionNoteWritersGuardTests stays green with the release transaction as an allowed writer.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">No live call. Never run python. Never --no-verify. No bare git stash.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The release transaction carries the column on the invoice update, writes no status, and a version fault applies neither update.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No note: the reason in the column, no Values key, byte-identical hash; the validation set of 2a.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The existing SubmissionOverrideServiceTests stay green; BFF build --warnaserror 0 warnings; ArchTests green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load the knowledge files first. Follow task-execute for rigor, checkpoints and quality gates.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
